      "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\sin x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/92ccbdbd54dc0d49f5cef42568749d4c5cda6065109e19e0c7b4cc75b5752a2c.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=3\\sin x.$",
